      "message": "Just checking here - if the intention os that this should be *all* aconfig declarations (similar to how we have one monolithic android flags jar shared for unbundled development) should it *also* include all aconfigs/API files from verticals? - i.e.\n\n```\n    api_files: [\n        \":frameworks-base-api-current.txt\",\n        \":frameworks-base-api-system-current.txt\",\n        \":frameworks-base-api-system-server-current.txt\",\n        \":frameworks-base-api-module-lib-current.txt\",\n        \":wear-sdk-api-current.txt\",\n        \":wear-sdk-api-system-current.txt\",\n        // and automotive etc...\n    ],\n```\n\nOnly caveat with that would be the output - would it still make sense to put finalized flag output in /prebuits/sdk/\u003cversion\u003e given that verticals have prebuilts in /prebuilts/sdk/opt/\u003cwear\u003e/\u003cversion\u003e etc?\n\nWould there be a way to filter/direct output based on namespace etc?\n\nNot looking to overcomplicate this, so sorry for piping up here, but very interested in ensuring that this is a tool that is useable across all developers of flagged api.",
